Subject: [PATCH] forward the toolchain to the nested vst3_helper configure

JUCE builds juce_vst3_helper as a separate CMake project and configures it at
build time.  That nested configure only received the compiler paths, so under a
cross-compile it saw the host platform and probed clang-cl as if it were native
("posix_spawn failed"), and the VST3 target died before linking.

Three more settings have to be forwarded: the toolchain file (so it is a Windows
configure at all), the cross-compiling emulator (so its try_run probes go through
wine), and the build type (otherwise it defaults to Debug, and the xwin splat
ships the release CRT only).

Upstream 8.0.13 does not do this.  Applied by Config/CMakeLists.txt when
cross-compiling for Windows, and only then -- a host build leaves the submodule
pristine.
---
--- a/extras/Build/CMake/JUCEUtils.cmake
+++ b/extras/Build/CMake/JUCEUtils.cmake
@@ -1106,6 +1106,22 @@
         list(APPEND PASSTHROUGH_ARGS "-DCMAKE_RC_COMPILER=${CMAKE_RC_COMPILER}")
     endif()
 
+    # Cross-compiling needs more than the compiler paths: the nested project
+    # configures from scratch, so without the toolchain file it sees the host
+    # platform and fails probing clang-cl ("posix_spawn failed").  The emulator
+    # lets the helper's try_run tests execute a target binary through wine.
+    if(CMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE)
+        list(APPEND PASSTHROUGH_ARGS "-DCMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE=${CMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE}")
+    endif()
+
+    if(CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING_EMULATOR)
+        list(APPEND PASSTHROUGH_ARGS "-DCMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING_EMULATOR=${CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING_EMULATOR}")
+    endif()
+
+    if(CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE)
+        list(APPEND PASSTHROUGH_ARGS "-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=${CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE}")
+    endif()
+
     add_custom_target(${helper_target}
         COMMAND "${CMAKE_COMMAND}"
             "-G${CMAKE_GENERATOR}"
